    "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/developing-today/code/pull/8020?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> ## Review failed\n> \n> The pull request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe CLI flag index now documents `--remote-file` for `exec` and `run`. The flag coverage exemptions note that inline-source probes do not cover named-script search-path resolution.\n\n**Changes: Remote-file flag index**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Flag documentation and coverage** <br> `pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/flagindex_generated.go`, `pkgs/mcpx/internal/cli/execflagcoverage.go`|The `exec` and `run` flag entries describe daemon-side script-name resolution with `--remote`. The coverage exemption notes the inline-source probe limitation and identifies tests that cover this behavior.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~5 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"a99ea2629c70b4d44d3a0543b4313dcef66f2582\" -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-unassessed-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Minimal</strong> · up to <code>a99ea</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `a99ea`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"a99ea2629c70b4d44d3a0543b4313dcef66f2582\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"a99ea2629c70b4d44d3a0543b4313dcef66f2582\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe flag documentation and coverage exemption match the implemented behavior. No merge-blocking defect is established; the suggested forwarding test can follow separately.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=developing-today/code&utm_content=8020)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Share</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%